{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2468 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fdc740b8aa9e293c29631e99c41ec2adef5473e2d7e3b92d9c9dd238b094789a" :edb/db-before-t 2467 :edb/db-after-t 2468 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535780 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:07:09.063Z" 13194139535780 true] [17592186175872 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365930 13194139535780 true] [17592186175872 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365937 13194139535780 true] [17592186175880 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365923 13194139535780 true] [17592186175880 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365944 13194139535780 true] [17592186176425 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535780 true] [17592186176425 1100 "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=0$\n- The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$\n- The series diverges at $x=2$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186176425 1100 "The power series $∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}(x - \\frac{1}{2})^{n}$ converges at $x =-1$. Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n1. The series converges at $x = 0$\n2. The series converges at $x =-\\frac{3}{2}$\n3. The series diverges at $x = 2$" 13194139535780 false] [17592186176425 1145 "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{3}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{3}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/03901ede0b4fadb59556c63aa4534b3a9e20c1e8188388e6256434ece03d9211.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $0\\in [-1,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365924 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1089 "q-103150" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1100 "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=-5$\n- The series converges at $x=-2$\n- The series converges at $x=1$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1113 #uuid "ec34b3f9-f746-52c7-8ca3-5de14cc8b3a9" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365923 1145 "The center of the expansion is $x=-3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-5,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-5,-1].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/7d68a4bd81717c3ad663fc85c45dfce62217a046f683cc92a6869f87ff3b166a.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $-2\\in (-5,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $1\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365925 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365926 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365927 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365928 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365929 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1041 "selection" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365929 13194139535780 true] [17592186365924 1110 #uuid "261de739-ef95-530e-af64-b6998f17f912" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365925 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365925 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365925 1111 #uuid "32282dea-b17d-5d30-8790-c81d3298c5fd" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365926 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365926 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365926 1111 #uuid "703950ce-79f0-571a-a3ad-e8c92fc321e1" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365927 1034 "I only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365927 1111 #uuid "bbe935d6-4e1b-5f7e-8091-b06a6835a130" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365928 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365928 1111 #uuid "9a0b5829-3986-50f2-a5ac-00aa4f84e6dd" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365929 1034 "II only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365929 1111 #uuid "512ccae2-2ef3-5111-a276-1fc8cb7aef86" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365931 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1089 "q-10949" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1100 "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}{n!}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1113 #uuid "37e2ef5f-52a9-5810-a866-d25a6434c7cf" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365930 1145 "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}{n!}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{2}^{n+1}(x-1)^{n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\cdot \\frac{n!}{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{2(x-1)}{n+1}| \\\\  & =2|x-1|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{n+1} \\\\  & =2|x-1|\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCondition of convergence $L<1$ is satisfied for all $x\\in I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, which is the interval of convergence in this case. The radius of convergence is $R=\\infty .$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365932 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365933 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365934 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365935 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365936 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1041 "selection" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365934 13194139535780 true] [17592186365931 1110 #uuid "c8b5b4f1-d3f3-5f3a-92d9-af81785db125" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365932 1034 "$R=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $I=(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365932 1111 #uuid "434eaf26-d1a9-579b-8e14-849a65caf76c" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365933 1034 "$R=\\infty $ and $I=(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365933 1111 #uuid "7582e5b5-d637-566b-b7db-97b68fa9e306" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365934 1034 "$R=\\infty $ and $I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365934 1111 #uuid "9bc2cdb0-3689-5c36-9e68-d90929ab14d8" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365935 1034 "$R=2$ and $I=(-1,1)$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365935 1111 #uuid "9df29785-afed-5fe7-adb8-aa8062ab27a4" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365936 1034 "$R=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $I=(0,1)$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365936 1111 #uuid "f6323197-75d5-5798-a0f0-5cebf78339a4" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365938 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1089 "q-13912" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1100 "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1113 #uuid "4c54e973-6e64-50b6-b096-4b16776e42ab" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365937 1145 "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x-1)^{3(n+1)}}{(n+1)^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{n}^{3}}{(x-1)^{3n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{n}^{3}(x-1)^{3}}{(n+1)^{3}}| \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n}{n+1})}^{3} \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-1{|}^{3} & <1 \\\\ |x-1| & <1 \\\\ -1<x-1 & <1 \\\\ 0<x & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $R=1,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(0,2).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x-1|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=0$ and $x=2$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\n- When $x=2$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(2-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the $p$-series test.\n\nConsequently, the interval of convergence is $I=[0,2].$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365939 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365940 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365941 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365942 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365943 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1041 "selection" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365942 13194139535780 true] [17592186365938 1110 #uuid "91d818ba-bd42-5be3-b740-03c5c3181697" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365939 1034 "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2]$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365939 1111 #uuid "3cceb71f-d7c8-545e-aa1b-da9d0be4cc89" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365940 1034 "$R=\\infty $ and  $I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365940 1111 #uuid "3386aa4f-1a8d-5a39-bf78-987f8bc4f2c1" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365941 1034 "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2)$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365941 1111 #uuid "a85a2725-9592-593f-a2f2-f265d597d1a8" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365942 1034 "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2]$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365942 1111 #uuid "64cbf145-03f1-5fbd-ae61-a610ccd2e1bf" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365943 1034 "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2)$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365943 1111 #uuid "53e34974-caa0-599e-8be0-4d193ed95a38" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365945 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1089 "q-50871" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1100 "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=0.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=1$\n- The series diverges at $x=4$\n- The series diverges at $x=-2$" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1113 #uuid "1407a663-14cb-5262-82d0-8dc686ad5604" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365944 1145 "The center of the expansion is $x=2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=0,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[0,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[0,4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/a56e24009403f0177f608ba932c03ab77e8db35e1db3e1221c4fb49efca7219f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $1\\in [0,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $4\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-2\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365946 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365947 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365948 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365949 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365950 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1041 "selection" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365948 13194139535780 true] [17592186365945 1110 #uuid "39c198d6-8d7c-57da-af05-12cae403c077" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365946 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365946 1111 #uuid "4fa7366b-f3de-5758-830b-437ae25b3afc" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365947 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365947 1111 #uuid "9aeabdca-9c2d-5ebf-ad81-a61d33bf8eac" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365948 1034 "I only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365948 1111 #uuid "c22f9eb3-e464-5cb8-aacc-e302d005f5f0" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365949 1034 "III only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365949 1111 #uuid "8f1d1bbd-5948-5b3f-bad9-c21f73b84442" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365950 1034 "II only" 13194139535780 true] [17592186365950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535780 true] [17592186365950 1111 #uuid "9c401994-b0bb-519d-9265-a62c93ede275" 13194139535780 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-103150" 17592186365923 "q-103150/selection" 17592186365924 "q-103150/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186365925 "q-103150/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186365926 "q-103150/selection/5b26512916